      "math_academy_id": "q-17357",
      "knowledge_point_id": "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Cosine Function",
      "problem": "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x+{50}^{∘})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=-{1}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘},\\,x={b}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $b?$",
      "worked_solution": "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+{50}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & 5x+{50}^{∘} & ={315}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & =-{5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & 5x & ={265}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ x & =-{1}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={53}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b=53.$",
