      "math_academy_id": "q-121066",
      "knowledge_point_id": "97786302-e865-5581-b08e-8da7c6b7a01b",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function",
      "problem": "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +\\frac{n\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$",
      "worked_solution": "The given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{18}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=-\\frac{1}{18}.$",
